00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:38.070
we're able to expose that so
that then you can make use

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:43.320
of those MCP tools elsewhere
in your development frame.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:44.790
One key thing to stress here,

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:47.280
this is a.NET
framework application

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:50.340
that we've built years
ago, but you know

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:53.640
that there are capabilities
with inside that web API

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:55.170
that you now want to expose

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:58.870
to more modern
development frameworks.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:02.820
Agentic Applications Patterns.

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:05.220
So with inside
Azure App Service,

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:08.670
we can host your
agent-based modular design.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:12.780
So agentic applications use
specialized agents responsible

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:13.860
for distinct domains.

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:18.030
So maybe you have an agent
for your sales management,

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:22.860
maybe you have a product agent,
maybe you have a shipping agent,

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:26.880
and they expose different
functionality directly

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:29.130
for different
domains, therefore,

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:32.580
more modular and task-focused.

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:34.410
With agentic application design,

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:37.470
we often see orchestrated
coordination happening

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:41.970
between those various agents,
so that when requests come

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:46.110
into that orchestrator,
it is able to determine

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:49.080
which is the most efficient
execution sequence

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:50.250
and which agents need

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:54.420
to be involved throughout
those interactions.

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:56.670
By having them modular
and having them split

00:15:56.670 --> 00:15:59.760
into individual
task-focused agents,

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:04.560
this offers much more granular
scalability that means

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:08.580
that as the user demands evolve,

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:13.410
then your scaling can
flex to those needs.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.390
We are also going to show,
as we have mentioned

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:16.710
in the previous slide, the fact

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:21.960
that agentic design doesn't just
require brand new Greenfield

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.540
projects with the
brand new languages

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:27.090
with the latest versions.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:31.680
You can integrate directly with
both existing legacy systems

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:35.520
and brand new
Greenfield systems.

